-- ============================================================================
-- DR6 ASSOCIATE DEEP SEED: Casing & Tubing Design, beginner tier.
--
-- Six modules, 26 lessons, 132 questions (15 per module bank plus a 42
-- question final exam). The structure row is GENERATED from the tier's
-- manifest.json rather than hand typed, so the seeded structure and the
-- shipped lesson files cannot disagree.
--
-- What this tier owns: the tubular and its four ratings. Outside diameter,
-- wall, bore and a nominal weight that is a LABEL rather than a computed
-- quantity. Ten grades, of which the engine reads exactly one property, the
-- yield strength, so L-80 and N-80 are the same pipe to every formula here and
-- are not the same pipe in sour service. Barlow with the 12.5 percent wall
-- undertolerance, which costs exactly 0.875 on every row at every grade and
-- appears in burst and nowhere else. Pipe body yield, the one exact rating in
-- the course. Joint strength as a screening efficiency the catalog itself
-- calls a customary planning value. And the API Bulletin 5C3 FOUR-regime
-- collapse system, its three coefficient polynomials, its three D over t
-- boundaries and the axial-adjusted yield that combined loading feeds it.
--
-- THE FINDING THE CATALOG'S OWN OUTPUT PRODUCES, AND m05 IS BUILT ON. Of the
-- 28 catalog rows, exactly ONE gives the same collapse rating at all ten
-- grades: the 20 inch 94 lb/ft row, at 3554024.408995863 Pa, from H-40 through
-- Q-125 without moving. Its D over t of 45.662100456621005 is above the
-- transition-to-elastic boundary at every grade, and the elastic formula has
-- no yield strength in it. Over the same ten grades its burst spans a factor
-- of exactly 3.125 and its pipe body yield spans the same factor. Strength
-- varies by three across that table; stiffness does not vary at all, and
-- buckling is a stiffness problem. The 20 inch 106.5 row very nearly manages
-- it too: nine of its ten grades agree and only H-40 breaks the pattern.
--
-- A SECOND FINDING, IN m04. The combined-loading derating is only as strong as
-- the formula's dependence on the yield strength. In the yield regime it
-- passes through EXACTLY: on the 7 inch 35 lb/ft joint at K-55 the collapse
-- lost and the yield lost add to one at every fraction to fifteen decimals.
-- In the elastic regime it does nothing at all: the 20 inch 94 lb/ft joint at
-- K-55 is immune to tension up to 0.5465081838176975 of yield, and then loses
-- 0.003124397190863104 at a fraction of 0.6. And what a higher grade buys on
-- such a pipe is not collapse but IMMUNITY: H-40 leaves the regime at about
-- 0.27 of yield and Q-125 at about 0.84.
--
-- Every number in the lessons is derived by running the vendored
-- engines/drilling tubularDesign module and its tubular catalog against
-- tubular_cases.json, and the teaching lab the panels and this course share is
-- pinned by casingTubingLab.test.js. A numeric sweep over the lessons resolved
-- all 501 literals carrying seven or more significant figures to an
-- engine-derived value; a tier-leakage sweep over the lessons and the banks
-- reports zero downward leaks and zero same-tier answer prints against all
-- eighteen graded fields.
--
-- Answer keys live only here and in academy_quiz_questions, which has no
-- client SELECT policy.
-- ============================================================================

values ('casingtubing', 'beginner', '{"modules":[{"key":"m01-what-a-casing-string-is","title":"What a Casing String Is","lesson_keys":["l01-a-well-is-a-nest-of-pipes","l02-od-wall-id-and-weight","l03-grade-is-a-yield-strength","l04-what-a-rating-is-and-is-not"]},{"key":"m02-burst-and-tension","title":"Burst and Tension","lesson_keys":["l01-barlow-and-the-thin-wall-idea","l02-the-twelve-and-a-half-percent","l03-pipe-body-yield","l04-the-connection-is-the-weak-point","l05-burst-is-linear-in-the-grade"]},{"key":"m03-the-four-collapse-regimes","title":"The Four Collapse Regimes","lesson_keys":["l01-collapse-is-not-one-formula","l02-the-d-over-t-ratio","l03-the-four-formulas","l04-the-boundaries-belong-to-the-grade","l05-reading-the-regime-off-a-row"]},{"key":"m04-combined-loading","title":"Combined Loading","lesson_keys":["l01-tension-eats-collapse","l02-the-axial-adjusted-yield","l03-tension-moves-the-regime","l04-where-the-derating-bites","l05-when-the-yield-is-exhausted"]},{"key":"m05-reading-a-rating-table","title":"Reading a Rating Table","lesson_keys":["l01-the-elastic-regime-does-not-know-the-grade","l02-what-a-higher-grade-actually-buys","l03-minimum-wall-nominal-weight","l04-screening-numbers-and-data-sheets"]},{"key":"m06-the-associate-reading","title":"The Associate Reading","lesson_keys":["l01-the-story-so-far","l02-working-the-capstone","l03-onward"]}]}'::jsonb, 1)
